hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:
"2992","Abu Bakr (RA) said: \The narration of al-Thawri from 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay' from Anas (RA) from this chapter has already been dictated by me before.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""""
"2993","Narrated to us al-Sana'ani: Narrated to us al-Mu'tamir who said: I heard 'Abd Allah [ibn 'Umar al-'Umari] on the authority of Nafi' on the authority of Ibn 'Umar (RA) who said:\n\The Prophet of Allah (ﷺ) stayed at al-Batha' on the evening of the Day of Nahr (10th of Dhu al-Hijjah). Abu Bakr (RA) and 'Umar (RA) used to do that (i.e."","" pray there)"","" and Ibn 'Umar (RA) used to do it until he died. He would pray Zuhr"","" 'Asr"","" Maghrib"","" and 'Isha' there.\""\n\n**CHAPTER:**"""""
"2994","Narrated to us Ahmad ibn Mani‘, narrated to us al-Hasan ibn Musa, from Zuhayr, from Abu Ishaq, from Ibn Abi Juḥayfah, from his father who said:\n“I saw the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) pray the two rak‘ahs of the ‘Asr prayer at al-Abṭaḥ (al-Muḥaṣṣab).”\n\nAnd the report of ‘Amr ibn al-Ḥārith—from Qatādah—from Anas (RA) is to the same effect.\n\n**CHAPTER:**"
